{"name":"Light Glaze","hex":"#c0b5aa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"glaze","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The vitreous coating of pottery or porcelain; anything used as a coating or color in glazing.","A transparent or semi-transparent layer of paint."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To install windows.","To apply a thin, transparent layer of coating."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glaze"}],"entries":[{"title":"Glaze (ice)","blocks":[{"text":"Glaze or glaze ice, also called glazed frost or verglas, is a smooth, transparent and homogeneous ice coating occurring when freezing rain or drizzle hits a surface. It is similar in appearance to clear ice, which forms from supercooled water droplets. It is a relatively common occurrence in temperate climates in the winter when precipitation forms in warm air aloft and falls into below-freezing temperature at the surface."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Ice_on_grass.jpg/330px-Ice_on_grass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glaze_(ice)","wikidata":"Q1192031"},{"title":"Glaze (painting technique)","blocks":[{"text":"A glaze is a thin transparent or semi-transparent layer on a painting which modifies the appearance of the underlying paint layer. Glazes can change the chroma, value, hue and texture of a surface. Glazes consist of a great amount of binding medium in relation to a very small amount of pigment. Drying time will depend on the amount and type of paint medium used in the glaze. The medium, base, or vehicle is the mixture to which the dry pigment is added. Different media can increase or decrease the rate at which oil paints dry."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glaze_(painting_technique)","wikidata":"Q1431523"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Trees_with_Ice.JPG/500px-Trees_with_Ice.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Trees_with_Ice.JPG/1280px-Trees_with_Ice.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Trees_with_Ice.JPG/500px-Trees_with_Ice.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Glazed tree branches are noted for both their beauty and their tendency to snap","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATrees_with_Ice.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Freezing_Rain_on_Tree_Branch.jpg/500px-Freezing_Rain_on_Tree_Branch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Freezing_Rain_on_Tree_Branch.jpg/1280px-Freezing_Rain_on_Tree_Branch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Freezing_Rain_on_Tree_Branch.jpg/500px-Freezing_Rain_on_Tree_Branch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Branch fully encapsulated in glaze","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFreezing_Rain_on_Tree_Branch.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Moscow_2010-2011_glaze_ice.jpg/500px-Moscow_2010-2011_glaze_ice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Moscow_2010-2011_glaze_ice.jpg/1280px-Moscow_2010-2011_glaze_ice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Moscow_2010-2011_glaze_ice.jpg/500px-Moscow_2010-2011_glaze_ice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A forest in Moscow a week after an incident of freezing rain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMoscow_2010-2011_glaze_ice.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG/500px-Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG/1280px-Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG/500px-Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai